## 8a. Platform revision order (Aug 4 2026 — P-010 / P-011)

Eval order on upload: **Agent Judge (Quality Check) before Difficulty**.

- If blocked with `Blocked at the agentic judge. Not run: difficulty screen…` → fix Judge axes only; Difficulty did not run.
- Blocking Judge axes: **test_coverage** / **test_faithfulness**.
- **Revision bar:** every Agent Judge axis **≥ 3.5** before treating Difficulty as in-scope (also fix any “3 with reservations”).
- Verdict `discuss (overreach)` → faithfulness: every graded/reward-gating assert must be stated or implied in the instruction; remove/ungrade **or** state the public contract (`P-011`). Do not dump file/helper walkthroughs to “satisfy” faithfulness.
- Coverage chase without instruction sync often flips the next Judge to overreach — move instruction ↔ tests ↔ oracle together.
- After Judge passes (≥3.5): Difficulty uses **4 trials per model** (not 8); worse model must still be **≤50%** pass rate.
- Do not invent Difficulty results when Judge blocked the screen.

## 8b. Recurring traps promoted Aug 2026 (≥2 sightings)

- Prefer trimming untested instruction claims over thin f2p filler (`P-006`).
- Compiler-build verifiers often need higher `verifier.timeout_sec` within 1800 (`P-007`).
- Hard-fail missing build tools instead of `SkipTest` soft-pass (`P-008`).
- Mode-only dirty trees → `git reset --hard` + reflog cleanup; not Invalid (`P-009`).
- Agent Judge fails before Difficulty runs → revise Judge first (`P-010`).
- `discuss (overreach)` / axis below 3.5 → sync instruction↔tests; target ≥3.5 before Difficulty (`P-011`).

